{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "15700440",
      "title": "Starting Project & Why You Would Replace Redux",
      "sourceHash": "dbf09dd8b126abf929c3567ab0db1a47832be714cbe742b62f4fa277aadea404",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 3.81,
          "en": "For this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.81,
          "end": 5.6,
          "en": "I have prepared a little demo project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.6,
          "end": 8.4,
          "en": "which you will find attached to this lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.4,
          "end": 10.05,
          "en": "And this project, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.05,
          "end": 13.06,
          "en": "renders this very simple application here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.06,
          "end": 16.33,
          "en": "where we got a list of fictional products",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.33,
          "end": 18.31,
          "en": "and we got a favorites section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.31,
          "end": 20.04,
          "en": "and we can basically switch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.04,
          "end": 22.08,
          "en": "between these pages and we can mark something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.08,
          "end": 24.66,
          "en": "as a favorite here in the all products page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.66,
          "end": 27.09,
          "en": "and then see it here, and well obviously,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.09,
          "end": 29.42,
          "en": "also get rid of that favorite status, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.42,
          "end": 33.22,
          "en": "So a very trivial app, but an app where I use Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.22,
          "end": 34.896,
          "en": "to manage this favorite status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.896,
          "end": 36.92,
          "en": "I use Redux here because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 36.92,
          "end": 39.63,
          "en": "we need to state in two different pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 39.63,
          "end": 43.06,
          "en": "and that would be harder to do with props only.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.06,
          "end": 45.5,
          "en": "And in addition, as I already covered throughout the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 45.5,
          "end": 47.76,
          "en": "I don't want to pass all the state through",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 47.76,
          "end": 50.09,
          "en": "multiple layers of components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 50.09,
          "end": 52.61,
          "en": "just so that I have it everywhere where I need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 52.61,
          "end": 55.26,
          "en": "And Redux is really convenient for such cases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.26,
          "end": 57.3,
          "en": "it's a great state management tool",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 57.3,
          "end": 59.13,
          "en": "when you have some global state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 59.13,
          "end": 60.6,
          "en": "And a list of products,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 60.6,
          "end": 63.33,
          "en": "and favorited products would be a great example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 63.33,
          "end": 67.68,
          "en": "if you're building a more complete online shop, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 67.68,
          "end": 70.32,
          "en": "Now in this relatively simple project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 70.32,
          "end": 71.88,
          "en": "which of course is simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 71.88,
          "end": 75.122,
          "en": "so that we can focus on Redux and how to replace it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 75.122,
          "end": 78.78,
          "en": "there I used the traditional Redux approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 78.78,
          "end": 80.09,
          "en": "I showed you in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 80.09,
          "end": 83.23,
          "en": "here I have my product reducer with some initial state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 83.23,
          "end": 85.27,
          "en": "which initializes my products,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 85.27,
          "end": 87.46000000000001,
          "en": "every product has an ID, a title, a description,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 87.46000000000001,
          "end": 89.01,
          "en": "and a favorite status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 89.01,
          "end": 93.07,
          "en": "And then in the reducer, I watch for one action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 93.07,
          "end": 95.67,
          "en": "where I basically switch that favorite status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 95.67,
          "end": 98.00999999999999,
          "en": "off the product and invert it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 98.00999999999999,
          "end": 99.787,
          "en": "and assign a new state, thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 99.787,
          "end": 102.86,
          "en": "In my actions file, I have to do one action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 102.86,
          "end": 105.18,
          "en": "where we, well, have a action type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 105.18,
          "end": 106.96000000000001,
          "en": "and then also the ID of the product,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 106.96000000000001,
          "end": 108.6,
          "en": "which should be switched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 108.6,
          "end": 111.7,
          "en": "That is connected here to the products.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 111.7,
          "end": 113.4,
          "en": "which is our products page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 113.4,
          "end": 115.94,
          "en": "With the help of the useSelector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 115.94,
          "end": 119.21000000000001,
          "en": "hook added by react-Redux version seven or higher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 119.21000000000001,
          "end": 122.33,
          "en": "which I have covered at the end of the module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 122.33,
          "end": 125.86,
          "en": "where we transform our burger builder to use hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 125.86,
          "end": 128.78,
          "en": "There I covered this hook too, at the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 128.78,
          "end": 130.31,
          "en": "And this hook is simply used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 130.31,
          "end": 132.42,
          "en": "to select a slice of our state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 132.42,
          "end": 136.8,
          "en": "The shop slice, which we create in index.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 136.8,
          "end": 138.78,
          "en": "here by combining our reducers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 138.78,
          "end": 140.64,
          "en": "or, well our one reducer here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 140.64,
          "end": 142.28,
          "en": "But again, this is an example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 142.28,
          "end": 144.073,
          "en": "that could be part of a bigger app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 145.262,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "And then here, we select the products list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 149.34,
          "en": "from that slice and I'll put it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 149.34,
          "end": 150.55,
          "en": "That's what I'm doing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 150.55,
          "end": 153.66,
          "en": "In the favorites.js file, I also select something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 153.66,
          "end": 155.42000000000002,
          "en": "with useSelector from my store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 155.42000000000002,
          "end": 157.74,
          "en": "I select all products that are a favorite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 157.74,
          "end": 159.61,
          "en": "so that I can output them there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 159.61,
          "end": 162.63,
          "en": "And last, but not least, in the productitem.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 162.63,
          "end": 166.06,
          "en": "there is use the useDispatch hook provided by react-redux,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 166.06,
          "end": 168.87,
          "en": "so that when we click that favorite button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 168.87,
          "end": 171.46,
          "en": "we dispatch this toggleFav action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 171.46,
          "end": 175.09,
          "en": "which is defined in the actions folder of our store folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 175.09,
          "end": 176.21,
          "en": "That's how this app works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 176.21,
          "end": 179.44,
          "en": "and the first important thing I really want to emphasize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 179.44,
          "end": 182.18,
          "en": "is that there's nothing wrong with that approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 182.18,
          "end": 185.67,
          "en": "You don't need to switch away from Redux at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 185.67,
          "end": 187.1,
          "en": "But maybe you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 187.1,
          "end": 189.16,
          "en": "And why would you?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 189.16,
          "end": 192.66,
          "en": "Well, maybe you want to stay in the react-only world,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 192.66,
          "end": 194.87,
          "en": "so that you don't need to learn Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 194.87,
          "end": 197.21,
          "en": "Arguably it's not that hard to learn Redux,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 197.21,
          "end": 199.23,
          "en": "but still, maybe you want to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 199.23,
          "end": 201.64,
          "en": "only the tools react gives you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 201.64,
          "end": 205.05,
          "en": "Maybe you also simply don't want to add that extra",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 205.05,
          "end": 208.18,
          "en": "Redux and react-redux library to your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 208.18,
          "end": 210.71,
          "en": "Hence, you would end up with a smaller bundle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 210.71,
          "end": 213.75,
          "en": "because if you don't have these extra libraries included,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 213.75,
          "end": 215.6,
          "en": "obviously you ship less code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 215.6,
          "end": 217.44,
          "en": "when you deploy your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 217.44,
          "end": 218.76,
          "en": "And that could be a good argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 218.76,
          "end": 221.32999999999998,
          "en": "because you can certainly shrink your bundle a bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 221.32999999999998,
          "end": 222.61,
          "en": "Though I will also say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 222.61,
          "end": 224.73,
          "en": "if you have a really large application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 224.73,
          "end": 227.7,
          "en": "it might not matter that much if it's included or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 227.7,
          "end": 229.17000000000002,
          "en": "Yet, that could be a reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 229.17000000000002,
          "end": 231.3,
          "en": "for why you don't want to use Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 231.3,
          "end": 233.06,
          "en": "Or you simply want to explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 233.06,
          "end": 236.02,
          "en": "how you can manage your state globally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 236.02,
          "end": 238.28,
          "en": "without passing everything through props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 238.28,
          "end": 240.74,
          "en": "but still without using Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 240.74,
          "end": 242.17,
          "en": "And that's why, in this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 242.17,
          "end": 244.41,
          "en": "I will now show you two different approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 244.41,
          "end": 248.083,
          "en": "of managing your state with react-only tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 248.083,
          "end": 250.66,
          "en": "One of those approaches is a good one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 250.66,
          "end": 252.38,
          "en": "the other one is not that great,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 252.38,
          "end": 254.25,
          "en": "at least, not for all use-cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 254.25,
          "end": 255.28,
          "en": "And I will show both,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 255.28,
          "end": 257.523,
          "en": "and I will explain when to use which.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}